{"content":[{"c":["BELIAL*, BELIAR*"],"sourceClass":"h1","t":"p"},{"c":["Common Hebrew noun meaning “baseness,” “worthlessness,” “wickedness,” or “lawlessness.” Belial, however, is often rendered as a proper noun. Thus, such translations as “sons of Belial” appear (",{"href":"?bref=Judg.19.22","r":"Judg.19.22","rawR":"Judg.19.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.19.22","value":"Judg.19.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 19:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.2.12","r":"1Sam.2.12","rawR":"1Sam.2.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.2.12","value":"1Sam.2.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 2:12"},", ",{"c":["kjv"],"sourceClass":"sc","t":"span"},"), “daughter of Belial” (",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.1.16","r":"1Sam.1.16","rawR":"1Sam.1.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.1.16","value":"1Sam.1.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 1:16"},"), or “children of Belial” (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.13.13","r":"Deut.13.13","rawR":"Deut.13.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.13.13","value":"Deut.13.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 13:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.20.13","r":"Judg.20.13","rawR":"Judg.20.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.20.13","value":"Judg.20.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 20:13"},"). Newer translations generally prefer the common noun form and give such readings as “worthless rabble” or simply “worthless” and the like (",{"href":"?bref=Deut.13.13","r":"Deut.13.13","rawR":"Deut.13.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Deut.13.13","value":"Deut.13.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"Dt 13:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.19.22","r":"Judg.19.22","rawR":"Judg.19.22","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.19.22","value":"Judg.19.22"}],"t":"ref","v":"Jgs 19:22"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Judg.20.13","r":"Judg.20.13","rawR":"Judg.20.13","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Judg.20.13","value":"Judg.20.13"}],"t":"ref","v":"20:13"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.1.16","r":"1Sam.1.16","rawR":"1Sam.1.16","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.1.16","value":"1Sam.1.16"}],"t":"ref","v":"1 Sm 1:16"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.2.12","r":"1Sam.2.12","rawR":"1Sam.2.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.2.12","value":"1Sam.2.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"2:12"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=1Sam.10.27","r":"1Sam.10.27","rawR":"1Sam.10.27","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"1Sam.10.27","value":"1Sam.10.27"}],"t":"ref","v":"10:27"},"; ",{"href":"?bref=Pr.6.12","r":"Pr.6.12","rawR":"Pr.6.12","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Pr.6.12","value":"Pr.6.12"}],"t":"ref","v":"Prv 6:12"},"). One possible exception to this rule is found in ",{"href":"?bref=Nah.1.15","r":"Nah.1.15","rawR":"Nah.1.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"Nah.1.15","value":"Nah.1.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"Nahum 1:15"},", which some scholars think should be rendered as “Belial,” a personalized designation of the Assyrian conqueror who had been a threat to the southern kingdom of Judah."],"sourceClass":"fl","t":"p"},{"c":["Intertestamental literature often used “Belial” as a proper noun and thus prepared the way for its NT usage. In the NT the term appears once as “Belial” (or Beliar in ",{"href":"?bref=2Cor.6.15","r":"2Cor.6.15","rawR":"2Cor.6.15","sourceRefs":[{"raw":"2Cor.6.15","value":"2Cor.6.15"}],"t":"ref","v":"2 Cor 6:15"},") and is identified with Satan, the personification of all that is evil. Noncanonical writings of the NT period commonly used it as a name for Satan or the Antichrist."],"sourceClass":"","t":"p"}],"format":"bsb-study-dictionary-v2","id":"BelialBeliar","provenance":{"archiveSha256":"10758ea00dbea7540f9337e43e59c8e4000295c1261e3426bab6f31c31dcff5b","release":"1.6","sourceCitationReferences":[{"anchorText":"Jgs 19:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.19.22","rawQueryValue":"Judg.19.22","sourceRefExact":"Judg.19.22"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 2:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.2.12","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.2.12","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.2.12"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 1:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.1.16","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.1.16","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.1.16"},{"anchorText":"Dt 13:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.13.13","rawQueryValue":"Deut.13.13","sourceRefExact":"Deut.13.13"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 20:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.20.13","rawQueryValue":"Judg.20.13","sourceRefExact":"Judg.20.13"},{"anchorText":"Dt 13:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Deut.13.13","rawQueryValue":"Deut.13.13","sourceRefExact":"Deut.13.13"},{"anchorText":"Jgs 19:22","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.19.22","rawQueryValue":"Judg.19.22","sourceRefExact":"Judg.19.22"},{"anchorText":"20:13","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Judg.20.13","rawQueryValue":"Judg.20.13","sourceRefExact":"Judg.20.13"},{"anchorText":"1 Sm 1:16","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.1.16","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.1.16","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.1.16"},{"anchorText":"2:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.2.12","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.2.12","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.2.12"},{"anchorText":"10:27","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=1Sam.10.27","rawQueryValue":"1Sam.10.27","sourceRefExact":"1Sam.10.27"},{"anchorText":"Prv 6:12","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Pr.6.12","rawQueryValue":"Pr.6.12","sourceRefExact":"Pr.6.12"},{"anchorText":"Nahum 1:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=Nah.1.15","rawQueryValue":"Nah.1.15","sourceRefExact":"Nah.1.15"},{"anchorText":"2 Cor 6:15","canonicalization":"deferred_to_dictionary_mapping_workstream","hrefExact":"?bref=2Cor.6.15","rawQueryValue":"2Cor.6.15","sourceRefExact":"2Cor.6.15"}],"sourceItemFragmentSha256":"3bff5468afbbfad6142c71f335ea5e3f2901efbab6987e6f8d2043dfd3746426","sourceItemName":"BelialBeliar","sourceItemOrder":162,"sourceMember":"Articles/B.xml","supplementPointersNotIncludedAsContent":[]},"sourceAttributes":{"name":"BelialBeliar","product":"TyndaleOpenBibleDictionary","typename":"Article"},"sourceTitleExact":"Belial*, Beliar*","title":"Belial*, Beliar*","version":"v2-a101d843a2f0cd3fc0c6"}